From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Muthukumar <muthukumardce@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Mar 2026 20:19:09 +0530
Subject: Fix fingerprint signal mismatches: canvas noise, RTT, voices,
 Widevine, history, window property order
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Address multiple fingerprint.com (fpjs) signal discrepancies between
Electron and Chrome to reduce bot/automation detection scores.

Canvas (canvasFingerprint):
- Disable Chromium's canvas noise protection in MaybeNoiseSnapshot() by
  returning false early. The noise injection alters pixel data causing
  canvas hashes to diverge from Chrome on the same GPU/machine.

History (history.length):
- Return 1 from both length() and lengthForBinding() to match Chrome's
  per-tab navigation count. Electron's BackForwardLength() accumulates
  entries across sessions (e.g. 150-200), which is abnormal.

Network RTT/downlink (s104 - navigator.connection.rtt):
- Return 50ms RTT and 10 Mbps downlink when not observing, instead of
  NQE 4G defaults (175ms→200ms RTT). Desktop Chrome on WiFi/Ethernet
  accumulates real measurements quickly; the 200ms 4G default is
  unusual for desktop browsers.
- Disable per-process RTT randomization (GetRandomMultiplier returns
  1.0) so values are consistent across browser instances.

Speech synthesis voices (s160):
- Inject 19 Google Network TTS voices that Chrome bundles via its
  component extension but Electron does not include. Voices use UTF-8
  encoded names matching Chrome's manifest, including NBSP (U+00A0)
  after "Google" for zh-CN and zh-HK voices to match Chrome's exact
  codepoint signature [32,17,160,2].

Widevine DRM (s154 - navigator.requestMediaKeySystemAccess):
- Enable Widevine by default in widevine.gni (enable_widevine = true).
- Add //electron/* visibility to components/cdm/renderer/BUILD.gn so
  Electron's renderer can link against WidevineKeySystemInfo for direct
  renderer-side key system registration.

Window property enumeration order (s156 - windowGlobalKeys):
- After the "chrome" property is installed on the window global by the
  extensions bindings system, delete and re-add "WebAssembly" so it
  appears immediately after "chrome" in Object.getOwnPropertyNames().
  This matches Chrome's property order ["Iterator","chrome","WebAssembly"]
  instead of Electron's default ["Iterator","chrome","cookieStore"].

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

